content.content:
   "AVFoundation can write this row": `null` is what routes an export to
   the frame-by-frame ImageIO writer (the two image formats), and since
   AVFoundation publishes no LPCM export preset the two new rows repeat the
   M4A row's name rather than carrying a null that would hand a WAV to the
   image writer. Read it as a record, never as an instruction.

   One row, `av1` (spec 11 CX-12, CX-14), is encoded at 10 bits by a library
   bundled in the app rather than by AVFoundation, which still writes its
   MP4 (its `avf_preset` is the passthrough name, a record): it and
   `av1_webm` alone carry `writer` ("svt_av1", the encoder route) and
   `encoder_speeds` (["faster",
   "balanced", "smaller"], the speeds its `encoder_speed` override takes),
   and like `hevc_10bit`, `prores_422` and `prores_4444` it carries `hdr`
   (spec 11 HD-14). `av1_webm` (spec 11 CX-15) is the same encoding in a
   WebM the core writes (`rc_webm_*`), with Opus sound: it carries the same
   `writer`, `encoder_speeds` and `hdr`, and its passthrough `avf_preset`
   records that the composition is read back through AVFoundation.
   `vp9_webm` (spec 11 CX-16) is VP9 from bundled libvpx in that WebM, 8-bit
   for an SDR picture and 10-bit for HLG and PQ: it carries `hdr` and
   `writer` ("libvpx") and no `encoder_speeds`, libvpx having one speed. */
char *rc_export_presets(void);

/* The output sizes the export sheet offers for `preset_id` against this
   project, as a JSON array of {id, name, width, height} in menu order. The
   FIRST row is the default: the document's own size ("document"), or for an
   image format its cap ("preset"). On a row that needs even pixel dimensions
   — every row AVFoundation writes but `prores_4444` — the "document" row
   holds the canvas with an odd edge made one pixel smaller, the size the
   file will have, and is named "Document (even)" when that is not the
   canvas's own size; everywhere else it is named "Document size" and is the
   canvas as it is (spec §11 G-33). After it come the standard sizes fitted to
 * through any other row is composited onto black.
 *
 * In an HLG project every video row's settings carry `color`, the picture it
 * writes: "hlg", "pq" or "sdr" (spec 11 HD-14); an SDR project's and an
 * audio row's never do.
 *
 * A row a bundled encoder writes (`av1`, `av1_webm`, `vp9_webm`, spec 11
 * CX-12, CX-16) adds `writer` at the end ("svt_av1" or "libvpx"), and the two
 * AV1 rows then `encoder_speed` (the speed asked, else "balanced"); no other
 * row's settings carry either key, and `vp9_webm`'s carry no speed. */
char *rc_export_settings(const RcProject *p, const char *preset_id, const char *overrides_json,
                         char **err_out);

/* -------------------------------------------------------------- graphics */

/* The motion-graphics engine (road map 10 §5e), linked from the `graphic`
 * round(pre_skip / 48 kHz) and an 80 ms SeekPreRoll), Chapters (one edition,
 * language "und"), Clusters, Cues. A block's time is pts_ns rounded half up
 * to ms. Each declared track is queued, and the earliest head (video first
 * among equal times) is written only while every track not ended has one;
 * a layout with one track writes each packet as it arrives. A Cluster
 * starts at each video key and before 32,767 ms past its start; each
 * key-started Cluster is a CuePoint. Every call flushes before it returns. */
#define RC_WEBM_VIDEO 1u
#define RC_WEBM_AUDIO 2u

typedef struct RcWebm RcWebm; /* add/end/finish may run on several threads at once */

/* Creates the file at `path` and writes its header. NULL with a lowercase
 * sentence through `err_out` naming the value for: no video and no audio,
 * another codec_id, an empty or absent V_AV1 private, any V_VP9 private,
 * malformed hex, bits_per_channel other than 8 or 10, an mdcv that is
 * not 24 bytes or a clli that is not 4, a 0 size or an fps with a 0 term, a
 * sample_rate other than 48000, channels outside 1-2, a chapter that ends at
 * or before its start or starts at or past duration_ns, unreadable JSON, or
 * a path that cannot be created. Freed with rc_webm_free. */
RcWebm *rc_webm_open(const char *path, const char *layout_json, char **err_out);

/* Adds one packet of `track` (RC_WEBM_VIDEO or RC_WEBM_AUDIO) presented at
 * `pts_ns`; `key` marks a video key (every audio block is a key). A
 * `discard_padding_ns` above 0 writes the packet as a BlockGroup with that
 * DiscardPadding. False with the sentence through `err_out` for NULL, a
 * track not in the layout or ended, a negative pts or one not after the
 * track's last, a call after finish, or an I/O failure. */
bool rc_webm_add_packet(RcWebm *webm, uint32_t track, int64_t pts_ns, bool key,
                        int64_t discard_padding_ns, const uint8_t *bytes, size_t len,
                        char **err_out);

/* Ends `track`: no packet of it follows, and the others stop waiting for
 * it. False with the sentence through `err_out` for NULL, a track not in
 * the layout or already ended, or a call after finish. */
bool rc_webm_end_track(RcWebm *webm, uint32_t track, char **err_out);

/* Writes every queued packet, the Cues, the SeekHead and the Segment's size;
 * then the file is closed. False with the sentence through `err_out` for
 * NULL, a second finish, or an I/O failure. */
bool rc_webm_finish(RcWebm *webm, char **err_out);

/* Releases a writer. NULL-tolerant. An unfinished file is left as it is, for
 * the app to remove. */
void rc_webm_free(RcWebm *webm);

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------- agent */

/* C signature of the host tool handler. Called from the server thread for
 * every `tools/call`. Must return a CallToolResult JSON object allocated
 * with `rc_agent_string_create` (ownership passes back across the return),
//! resolver here as the same `width`/`height` overrides a script sends.
//!
//! Two of the presets name a format AVFoundation cannot write at all: an
//! animated GIF and an animated PNG are assembled frame by frame through
//! ImageIO. That changes nothing here except one field — those rows carry
//! no `avf_preset`, and a null `avf_preset` is Swift's signal to take the
//! image-sequence path instead of building a session. Everything else
//! (the size, the rate, the range, the file's UTI) is resolved identically,
//! because it means the same thing on either path.
//!
//! Three rows, `av1` (spec §11 CX-12), `av1_webm` (CX-15) and `vp9_webm`
//! (CX-16), are encoded by a bundled library and not by AVFoundation, which
//! still writes `av1`'s container (the core writes the two WebMs): their
//! `writer` names the route, and on the two AV1 rows `encoder_speed` names
//! SVT-AV1's speed; no other row's settings carry either key, and
//! `vp9_webm`'s carry no speed, libvpx having one (CX-3).
//!
//! The preset table is the single source of truth: [`presets`] serializes
//! it for the picker and [`Project::export_settings`] resolves against the
//! same rows, so a preset cannot exist in the menu and not in the resolver.
//!
//! How an override value is READ and REFUSED is `export_overrides.rs`,
//! and the rows themselves — the containers, and the presets written into
//! them — are `export_table.rs`. The vocabulary and the table: this file
//! is the design they serve and the resolution that brings the two of
//! them together against one project.

